  body: "# Self-employment alongside employed-earner work\n\n**Model-assisted source interpretation; unreviewed.
    No entitlement decision or executable rule.**\n\nThe captured definition of a self-employed earner
    contains territorial and employment-category conditions and notes that employed-earner work does not
    itself prevent a person also being self-employed.\n\n## Evidence and scope\n\n[DMG 86201, PDF page
    44](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/698462dd468d351e1406b4a7/dmgch86.pdf#page=44) supports
    this scoped proposal. The source PDF SHA-256 is `909d328088dda0b6a94e0fc671bfa41f6d300689ff02d6f8a0292e30172f9908`.\n\
    \nNo employment-status decision is made. Gainful employment, territorial treatment, disregarded contribution
    cases and the cited regulations require review.\n\nThe capture date, the publication page's update
    date and a date stated in the guidance have different meanings. Linked legislation and memos need
    their own provision, version and applicability review.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/self-employment
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source explicitly allows the two employment descriptions to coexist, so a single
      exclusive status flag would lose a stated distinction relevant to earnings.
    evidence:
    - page: page/86/0044
      quote: "86201 A S/E earner is a person who is gainfully employed\n\n\n1.   in GB and\n\n\n2.   in
        employment that is not employed earners employment.\n\n\nS/E earner includes people employed outside
        of GB in employment which would be classed as\nemployment as a S/E earner if the employment was
        in GB. It also includes people undertaking\nemployment as a S/E earner where that employment is
        disregarded when working out social security\n\ncontributions1.\n\n\nNote: A person may also be
        employed as an employed earner. This does not stop the person being S/E.\n\n\n               \
        \                                         1 SPC Regs, reg 17B; SS Ben (C of E) Regs, reg\n   \
        \                                                     2(1)"
      locator: DMG 86201
